' Manual repro for the "Essential file missing" error (Change 1627).
'
' This cannot be exercised by a normal automated compile, since the bug it
' guards against only shows up when a file listed in include\lowlevel.dat
' is missing from disk - not something a .gcb source file can express on
' its own. To verify by hand:
'
'   1. Rename include\lowlevel\usart.h (in the include tree the compiler
'      you are testing actually reads from - see its own /version output
'      for which install directory that is) to something else, e.g. test.h.
'   2. Compile this file. Expect a single, clean error:
'        Error: Essential file missing: <path>\usart.h (listed in lowlevel.dat)
'      and no other unrelated errors (in particular, no second error for a
'      trailing blank line in lowlevel.dat - Change 1627 also fixed that).
'   3. Rename usart.h back. Expect this file to compile normally again,
'      identical to any other ordinary HSerSend program.

#chip 16F877A, 20
#define USART_BAUD_RATE 9600
#define USART_TX_BLOCKING
#define USART_DELAY OFF

Dir PORTC.6 Out

Do
  HSerSend(65)
  Wait 100 ms
Loop
